x_documentation(x_inRegion,x_EnglishLanguage,"Location as a\nrelation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c\nlocated_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any\ngiven time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its\nexact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further\ninstance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the\nregion which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant\nand another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial\nregion occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.   \nNote that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact\nlocation between one continuant and another which obtains when r and\nr1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a\ncavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which\nobtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and\nuterus") :- x_cid(a65b125bc8c57c).
